From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/mediatek: let the MT6897 camera masters attach without their larb

The camera DMA engines of the MT6897 reach the multimedia IOMMUs through
SMI larb14, whose ports come up with their MMU bit set. Neither the larb nor
the camera SMI sub-commons behind it are described yet. Let masters on
larb14 attach the way the video coprocessor does: without a larb device,
and linked to the SMI common of the IOMMU instead, which keeps the IOMMU
powered while they run.
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/mtk_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/mtk_iommu.c
index 10e19d5c6..4a275a5cc 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/mtk_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/mtk_iommu.c
@@ -1775,8 +1775,12 @@ static const unsigned int mt6897_larb_region_msk[ARRAY_SIZE(mt6897_multi_dom)][M
 #endif
 };
 
-/* larb31 stands for the masters without a larb: see the binding header */
-#define MT6897_NOLARB_MSK	BIT(31)
+/*
+ * larb31 stands for the masters without a larb: see the binding header. larb14,
+ * the one of the camera DMA, is not described yet, so its masters attach the
+ * same way; its ports come up with the MMU on.
+ */
+#define MT6897_NOLARB_MSK	(BIT(31) | BIT(14))
 
 static const struct mtk_iommu_plat_data mt6897_data_disp = {
 	.m4u_plat	= M4U_MT6897,
